  "description": "The TENTH and LAST arm of the ten-way selection EVALUATE TRUE at :148-182, which is the one arm that cannot be reached without nine genuine failures first. SEL0001I through SEL0009I all arrive as spaces, so :149, :152, :155, :158, :161, :164, :167, :170 and :173 are each evaluated and each false, and only then does :176 match - an EVALUATE TRUE stops at its first true WHEN, so this case walks the whole ordered chain rather than sampling it, and WHEN OTHER at :179 is never reached (gate G30). :177 moves the cell into CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SEL-FLG and :178 moves TRNID10I - not TRNID09I - into CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SELECTED. That is the LAST-ELEMENT half of the 1-based-to-0-based boundary: the tenth COBOL row group is index nine of the Java row collection, so an off-by-one would echo the tenth cell while selecting the ninth transaction. case18 pins the same mapping at the FIRST element, and the two together bracket the table. Both fields being present, :183 is true and the inner EVALUATE matches WHEN 'S' at :186 - the upper half of a two-clause fall-through pair whose lower half is WHEN 's' at :187 - so the program hard-codes COTRN01C at :188, stamps its own identity at :189-190, MOVEs 0 to CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT at :191 and XCTLs at :192-195. In a stateless translation that transfer is a response field naming the next program and nothing more: no server-side forward, no redirect and no session, with the 160-byte commarea and the 58-byte CDEMO-CT00-INFO extension both travelling in the payload (gates G37 and G40). The inbound values are chosen so that all four overwrites are observable rather than merely asserted - CM00 becomes CT00, COMEN01C becomes COTRN00C, COTRN00C becomes COTRN01C and the context 1 becomes 0. Control leaves at :193, so everything after it is unreached: the TRNIDINI edit at :206-219, the MOVE -1 at :221, the page reset at :224 and PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD at :225. The page number therefore comes back as the 1 it arrived as and the next-page flag as the Y it arrived as, no STARTBR, READNEXT, READPREV or ENDBR is issued against TRANSACT, no map is sent, and both message channels hold the spaces :102-103 left. The cursor is still TRNIDINL because :105 sets it in MAIN-PARA before any branch is taken, not because :221 ran. Two names diverge from their sources and both are honoured verbatim under rule R1: COTRN00C LISTS transactions although the migrated class is TransactionMenuController, and COTRN01C VIEWS the selected transaction although its class is TransactionAddController - README.md:223 and the source headers both document CT01 as Transaction View (risk R-B). This case asserts the handoff only; it assumes nothing about an insert at the target. Statically derived by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl paragraph by paragraph and cross-checking app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy for the 350-byte record, app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY for the xxxI widths, app/bms/COTRN00.bms for the DFHMDF lengths and app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy for the commarea - never captured from a running COBOL program.",
